H('407.d.1.A',3,"A team designing a rain garden to filter runoff first writes down what the garden must do. This stage of the engineering design process is:","defining the problem",["testing the prototype","presenting results","manufacturing"],"Design begins by defining the need.")
H('407.d.1.A',4,"After a pilot filter clogs in testing, the team changes the design and tests again. This repeated cycle is called:","iteration",["termination","isolation","litigation"],"Iteration refines a design.")
H('407.d.1.B',3,"A town wants one project to cover stormwater, drinking water, and wastewater. Compared with a single-system project, its complexity is:","greater",["smaller","unchanged","zero"],"More systems add complexity.")
H('407.d.1.B',4,"A water project has funding for 10 workers but needs 25. This is a limit on its:","resources",["scope statement","ethics code","logo"],"Staff and money are resources.")
H('407.d.1.C',3,"Residents near a proposed treatment plant, the city council, and the state regulator all affect the design as:","stakeholders",["competitors","suppliers only","inspectors only"],"Stakeholders have an interest in the outcome.")
H('407.d.1.C',4,"A neighborhood group objects to the smell from a planned plant, so engineers add odor control. The group influenced the design as a:","stakeholder",["subcontractor","supplier","auditor"],"Stakeholder concerns shape requirements.")
