H('407.d.3.C',3,"A factory could save money by dumping untreated waste into a creek, but that would harm the ecosystem. An engineer's ethics code puts public welfare and the environment:","first",["last","never","after profit"],"Ethics codes put public welfare first.")
H('407.d.3.C',4,"An engineer finds that the cheapest plant design will raise river temperatures and harm fish. The best response is to:","propose a design that protects the river",["hide the finding","choose cost alone","blame the fish"],"Engineers weigh environmental harm honestly.")
H('407.d.3.D',3,"A dam gives electricity and flood control but changes fish habitat. This shows that solutions can have:","both benefits and harms",["no effects","only benefits","only harms"],"Solutions have mixed impacts.")
H('407.d.3.D',4,"Burning trash to cut landfill volume can solve one problem while adding:","air emissions",["more water","free land","less cost always"],"A fix can create a new impact.")
H('407.d.4.A',3,"To make a physical model of a river system, a team first needs to:","identify the key parts to represent",["sell the model","paint the model","ship the model"],"Models start with deciding what matters.")
